<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karl Philipp, Prince of Schwarzenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1771">1771</a>–<a href="/years/1820">1820</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Karl Philipp zu Schwarzenberg · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-schwarzenberg">House of Schwarzenberg</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karl Philipp, Prince of Schwarzenberg, was an Austrian field marshal and diplomat who commanded the Austrian auxiliary corps in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1812. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> joined the Sixth Coalition in 1813 he became commander-in-chief of the allied armies, which defeated Napoleon at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leipzig">Battle of Leipzig</a> in October 1813 and entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1814.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karl-philipp-prince-of-schwarzenberg.jpg" alt="Karl Philipp, Prince of Schwarzenberg" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karel_Filip_Schwarzenberg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Austria joined the Sixth Coalition in August 1813, and <b>Field Marshal Karl Philipp</b> zu Schwarzenberg commanded the Allied armies that won the Battle of Leipzig.</blockquote><a href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The family remained prominent: <b>Karl Philipp zu Schwarzenberg</b> commanded the allied armies at Leipzig in 1813, and Felix zu Schwarzenberg led the Austrian Empire's government after the 1848 revolution.</blockquote><a href="/state/principality-of-schwarzenberg">Principality of Schwarzenberg</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=48.21,16.37&amp;year=1802" aria-label="Vienna on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4931 477 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Karl Philipp, Prince of Schwarzenberg"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5381 747h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=48.21,16.37&amp;year=1802">What was here in 1802? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
